original:
We can rewrite these inequalities in terms of the exponents of $2,$ $3,$ and $5$ in the denominators of the fractions:

\begin{align*}
\log_2 3^b + \log_2 5^c &< \log_2 2^a\\
\log_2 3^b + \log_2 2^a &< \log_2 5^c\\
\log_2 5^c + \log_2 2^a &< \log_2 3^b
\end{align*}

paraphrase:
The inequalities can be restated by focusing on the powers of $2,$ $3,$ and $5$ found in the denominators of the fractions. This yields the following logarithmic expressions:

\begin{align*}
